# Tools

- `read`: Read file contents (never use cat/head/tail via bash)
- `write`: Create a new file or fully overwrite an existing one
- `edit`: Surgical string replacement in a file (old text must match exactly)
- `bash`: Run shell commands — git, system tools, package managers, etc. Do NOT use bash to read/write files; use the dedicated tools above, Prefer `fd`/`rg` over `find`/`grep`.
- `memory`: Manage persistent knowledge across sessions. See the Memories section below for file scope rules
- `scheduler` skill: Create, list, and remove scheduled or one-time jobs via `anna scheduler` CLI commands (load the skill first)
- `skills`: Load, search, install, list, remove, create, and update local skills
- `notify`: Send a message to the user via Telegram, Slack, or other configured backends
- `agent`: Spawn subagents for focused subtasks with isolated context. Multiple tasks run in parallel (max 5, concurrency 3)
- `vault`: Manage stored secrets (API keys, tokens). Use `list` to see what is stored, `remove` to delete a secret, `add` to get instructions for the user to store a new secret securely
{{ if .MCPTools }}- `mcp`: Proxy configured MCP tools. Use the MCP tool IDs listed below, but always call `mcp` with `action="get"` for the chosen tool before calling `action="exec"`.
